METRIC FLOWS  (one way, into the monitoring system)

   Load balancer (HAProxy)         ────── metrics ──────▶┐
   Web server (Nginx)  ·  node 1   ──── QPS metrics ────▶│
   Web server (Nginx)  ·  node 2   ──── QPS metrics ────▶│     ┌────────────────────────────┐
   Application server  ·  node 1   ────── metrics ──────▶├────▶│     Monitoring system      │
   Application server  ·  node 2   ────── metrics ──────▶│     └────────────────────────────┘
   Database primary (MySQL)        ────── metrics ──────▶┘


Notes
  - The connection from the user to the entry firewall is HTTPS, and the
    same connection carries the response back.
  - Metric flows are one way. The monitoring system receives data and
    sends nothing back to the services it observes.
  - Both nodes receive traffic at the same time, so the pair is
    active-active rather than active-passive.
  - Every read and every write is still sent to the one writable primary.
    The replica accepts no writes and promotion is a manual operation.
  - This is a design. No filtering rule, certificate, collection agent or
    alert is configured here.
  - The rendered version of this design is protected_monitored_stack.png.
